  "title": "Total Supply",
  "slug": "total-supply",
  "public": true,
  "classIri": "urn:ngm:class:total-supply",
  "domain": "blockchain",
  "definition": "Total Supply is the count of all tokens that have ever been created on a blockchain network, encompassing circulating tokens, locked or vested tokens, tokens held in treasury reserves, and any tokens that have been minted but not yet distributed\u2014but excluding permanently destroyed (burned) tokens. It differs from the maximum supply (the hard cap set by the protocol) and from circulating supply (tokens freely tradeable on secondary markets). Total supply is a fundamental parameter in tokenomics analysis used to assess inflation, dilution, and long-term value dynamics.",
